cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Please cite this software/data release and the accompanying RASC study. No DOI has yet been assigned to this local release."
type: software
title: "RASC midpoint: code, data and verification for secular modulation and long-time accuracy"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Villatoro
    given-names: Francisco R.
    affiliation: "Universidad de Málaga"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-4314-6213"
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Reproducibility artifact for renormalized asymptotic successive corrections
  of implicit midpoint. It includes archived and residual-checked numerical
  experiments, per-step algebraic certificates, complete recorded snapshots,
  reference integrations, symbolic and numerical regression tests, and scripts
  for rebuilding the numerical evidence. Long-time nonlinear error bounds are
  conditional; the NLS second-corrector diagnostics are finite-window results.
  The manuscript and its LaTeX sources are not included. Original data and
  documentation are licensed CC BY 4.0 as specified in DATA_LICENSE.
  Supported by Universidad de Málaga, project PPRO-B4-2026-004
  (Plan Propio de Investigación, Transferencia y Divulgación Científica).
keywords:
  - implicit midpoint
  - asymptotic successive correction
  - renormalization
  - relative equilibria
  - long-time integration
  - numerical reproducibility
